(ARG-35 — `--` stops flag processing (LANGUAGE.md:4688). `--verbose`
 before it is parsed as a flag; `-v` after it is not.
 Also covers: ARG-36 (tokens after `--` are treated as positional
 arguments — they appear in `all`) and ARG-37 (the manual's own example
 invocation, `myprog --verbose -- -v file.txt`, at 4443-4449).
 Note the separator's own fate, which the manual does not state: `--` is
 removed from the filtered view but kept in `raw`.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-35.vox -o p && ./p --verbose -- -v file.txt
 Args: --verbose -- -v file.txt
 expected output:
   verbose is 1
   ALL
   -v
   file.txt
   RAW
   --verbose
   --
   -v
   file.txt
)
a flag called verbose is "-v" or "--verbose", it is a boolean.
Parse flags.

Print "verbose is {verbose}".
Print "ALL".
Print each item from arguments's all.
Print "RAW".
Print each item from arguments's raw.
